updated_at":"2026-10-25T22:56:10Z"},{"id":676351152,"node_id":"RA_kwDONhAAJs4oUEyw","name":"jabridge_1.4.0_source.tar.gz.sha256","label":"","uploader":{"login":"Watchdog0x","id":84445039,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0NDQ1MDM5","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":95,"digest":"sha256:2d18abb5364e5a7d7c71674eb13ac630237707e8436fb84e0275ae46a6d1a2c3","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-10-25T22:56:11Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T22:56:11Z"},{"id":676351154,"node_id":"RA_kwDONhAAJs4oUEyy","name":"jabridge_1.4.0_source.tar.gz.sig","label":"","uploader":{"login":"Watchdog0x","id":84445039,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0NDQ1MDM5","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/pgp-signature","state":"uploaded","size":88,"digest":"sha256:3a2054a40243bc35128caa95a8ea4e65c3d7397438596340d1a097fad149a3c5","download_count":1,"created_at":"2026-10-25T22:56:11Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T22:56:11Z"},{"id":676351103,"node_id":"RA_kwDONhAAJs4oUEx_","name":"SHA256SUMS","label":"","uploader":{"login":"Watchdog0x","id":84445039,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0NDQ1MDM5","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":295,"digest":"sha256:0dedee493579262bb785b0823684227e538fb3cb90be65eae6e802e5cf80a772","download_count":2,"created_at":"2026-10-25T22:56:10Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T22:56:10Z"}],"body":"Jabridge can now find and connect headsets through the Link 390 USB model `0b0e:2e57`. You can also disconnect or forget a headset and turn automatic pairing on or off.\n\nTested by the contributor on Link 390 firmware 1.3.0 with Evolve2 55 firmware 1.2.13. Other compatible headsets are intended to work but still need confirmation. Other Link 390 USB variants do not get these new controls.\n\nFactory reset stays disabled on Link 390. Its Bluetooth radio and softphone settings stay read-only. Firmware updates were not tested in this change.\n\nThanks @shimonkohn for the code and hardware tests in [PR #53](https://github.com/Watchdog0x/jabridge/pull/53).\n\nUpdate Jabridge:\n\n```sh\njabridge update\n```\n\nFor package-managed installs, use your package manager.\n\nThen choose **Find headset**, put your headset in pairing mode and select it.\n","mentions_count":1}
